  "releaseNotes": "NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.ReclaimProtocolOASIS v2.0.3\n\nConnects the OASIS to Reclaim Protocol -- the privacy-first ZK attestation layer that lets users prove data from any HTTPS source without revealing it. OASIS avatars can attest to GitHub contributions, Twitter followers, bank balances, and more — all as verifiable ZK proofs. Part of the OASIS HOT-Swappable Provider Architecture. Ecosystem: https://oasisomniverse.one\n\nWhat's new since v2.0.2\n- docs: add README.md for 57 providers + bump submodule pointers (87b2b85)\n- feat: add 11 new OASIS providers — Maps (4), Blockchain (2), Network (3), Storage (2) (e1538d7)\n- feat(ReclaimProtocolOASIS): verify Reclaim zkTLS proofs like the official SDK (0853d66)\n- fix: resolve all build errors in 11 new OASIS providers (2d0a601)\n\nFull changelog\nhttps://github.com/NextGenSoftwareUK/OASIS/commits/master/Providers/Network/NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.ReclaimProtocolOASIS",
